# A local function scoped to a complex, in a model that also has a rule whose
# products are joined by ".".
#
# Bind attaches one B to each A. Flip turns A(s~0) into A(s~1) at k times the
# number of B in A's complex: zero while A is free, k once it is bound. So no A
# can flip before it binds and every A flips after it: Abound = 100 and
# Aon = 100 exactly by t=40, whatever the seed.
#
# Open has nothing to do with A or B. It is here because BioNetGen writes its
# products, D(x,y!+).E(x), as one pattern holding two molecules with no bond
# between them. NFsim's reader used to answer that by switching complex
# bookkeeping on, by which time the seed molecules already existed. Their
# complexes were then never merged when they bound, the function went on seeing
# no B, and Aon stayed at 0 with every A bound. It takes -no-bscb to show,
# because bookkeeping is otherwise on from the start.

begin model
begin parameters
  kon  0.1
  k    1.0
  kd   1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,s~0~1)
  B(a)
  D(x,y)
  E(x,y)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b,s~0)                100
  B(a)                    200
  D(x!1,y!2).E(x!1,y!2)   10
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Aon     A(s~1)
  Molecules  Abound  A(b!+)
  Molecules  Bs      B()
  Molecules  DEx     D(x!1).E(x!1)
end observables
begin functions
  nB(x) = Bs(x)
end functions
begin reaction rules
  Bind: A(b) + B(a) -> A(b!1).B(a!1)         kon
  Flip: %x::A(s~0) -> %x::A(s~1)             k*nB(x)
  Open: D(x!1,y!+).E(x!1) -> D(x,y!+).E(x)   kd
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
